      "content": "#include <algorithm>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <cstddef>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <memory>\n#include <vector>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    if (!(std::cin >> n >> s)) return 0;\n\n    assert(s < n);\n    assert(n < 8000);\n    assert(s > 0);\n    assert(n > 0);\n\n    const int retained_rows = std::min(s, n - s);\n    std::unique_ptr<int[]> history(\n        new int[static_cast<std::size_t>(retained_rows) * n]);\n    std::vector<int> row(n);\n    std::vector<long long> column_sums(n, 0);\n    long long best = 0;\n\n    for (int r = 0; r < n; ++r) {\n        for (int c = 0; c < n; ++c) {\n            std::scanf(\"%d\", &row[c]);\n        }\n\n        if (r < s) {\n            for (int c = 0; c < n; ++c) {\n                column_sums[c] += row[c];\n            }\n            // Only rows that eventually leave a window need storage.\n            if (r < n - s) {\n                int* saved = history.get() + static_cast<std::size_t>(r) * n;\n                std::copy(row.begin(), row.end(), saved);\n            }\n        } else {\n            int* outgoing = history.get()\n                + static_cast<std::size_t>((r - s) % retained_rows) * n;\n            if (r < n - s) {\n                // Here retained_rows == s, so the incoming row reuses this slot.\n                for (int c = 0; c < n; ++c) {\n                    column_sums[c] += static_cast<long long>(row[c]) - outgoing[c];\n                    outgoing[c] = row[c];\n                }\n            } else {\n                for (int c = 0; c < n; ++c) {\n                    column_sums[c] += static_cast<long long>(row[c]) - outgoing[c];\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        if (r + 1 < s) continue;\n\n        long long window_sum = 0;\n        for (int c = 0; c < s; ++c) {\n            window_sum += column_sums[c];\n        }\n        if (r + 1 == s) {\n            best = window_sum;\n        } else {\n            best = std::max(best, window_sum);\n        }\n        for (int c = s; c < n; ++c) {\n            window_sum += column_sums[c] - column_sums[c - s];\n            best = std::max(best, window_sum);\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::printf(\"%lld\\n\", best);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Streaming rows through a compact history ring should improve locality and reduce allocation traffic while retaining O(N^2) rolling-window computation and unchanged input parsing.",
